      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T09:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code is reimplementing some of the behaviour of canBypassNetworkPermissionsCheck, which means that if someone changes canBypassNetworkPermissionsCheck without changing this code, they could introduce a bug.\n\nIs there something we can do to make the two methods share more code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9106,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 9106,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "48497a04_9830fdf4",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 9106,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T22:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I double checked the code, and I believe the overlap between canBypassNetworkPermissionsCheck and handleUidCarrierPrivilegesLost is that they both call hasCarrierPrivilegeForNetworkCaps(), the rest are different, since now we removed hasCarrierPrivilegeForNetworkCaps() in handleUidCarrierPrivilegesLost, I don\u0027t think there are more code to be shared between the two methods",
      "parentUuid": "458aabca_cd281846",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9106,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 9106,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2418f937_305614d9",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 9115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T09:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a race condition here: this code calls synchronously into CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator based on state (the uid being passed into the method) that is no longer current in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.\n\nAs an example of possibly-incorrect behaviour: if a UID loses and then immediately re-gains carrier privilege, then we might not declare its request unfulfillable because by the time handleUidCarrierPrivilegesLost is called for that UID, hasCarrierPrivilegeForNetwork might have already started returning true for that UID. This behaviour sounds relatively harmless but there are probably other issues that may be more severe.\n\nIn order to fix these races for good I think we\u0027ll have to move CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the ConnectivityService handler thread, which I think it something we should do anyway.\n\nPer discussion, if we just want a simple change for now we might be able simply to remove the call to hasCarrierPrivilegeForNetworkCaps.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9115,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 9115,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
