    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3283fe0d_efed23bf",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T09:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why support more than one listener? CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator is a singleton which is only used by CS. Seems easier to have the owner of this class (ConnectivityService) pass in a \"callback\" lambda (or just a BiConsumer\u003cInteger\u003e or Consumer\u003cPair\u003cInteger\u003e\u003e to the constructor. That can be made private final.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "888a741a_4f6dcc3d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T22:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I changed the implementation to only support one listener which will be passed in through the constructor. I didn\u0027t change the listener into Consumer because I didn\u0027t use that before, so I need to check some example code in order to do that. I can draft another CL for that if you insist.",
      "parentUuid": "3283fe0d_efed23bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0d96aef_7fddfad0",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T09:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just passing in the UID is not useful here, because without knowing the subId, CS cannot determine which network(s) the UID lost privileges on. You might be able to fix this by passing both the UID and the subId it lost privileges on.\n\nOr, you could just pass in nothing at all and have CS recalculate everything. I think that to do this, you\u0027ll need to move CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the CS handler thread (see comment below). That\u0027s a larger change though; not sure if we want to do that in this CL.\n\nIdeally, we would have moved CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the CS handler thread *first*, and then made this change. But if we need to submit this CL soon, then maybe we can fix the problem in this CL by passing in both subId and uid, and then move CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the CS handler thread in another CL?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7c08e2e_d3b47135",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T22:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe our intention is, whenever the UID loses Carrier Privileges, we want to clear all the restricted network requests which are owned by the UID, and also remove the UID from the allowedUiD list of the corresponding networks. Since a Carrier app should only be allowed to access its own restricted networks, cleaning all the requests owned by the UID should be enough?",
      "parentUuid": "a0d96aef_7fddfad0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cd93e74_9e7e4895",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-07T01:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When device has two slot and for example,\nslot1 is linked to subId1, uid0\nslot2 is linked to subId2, uid0\n\nif the slot1’s uid is updated to uid1, should not uid0 keep the CarrierPrivilege for subId2?\nOr is it impossible that the single uid has privilege for multiple subIds?",
      "parentUuid": "d7c08e2e_d3b47135",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1666b5c9_3a2375b0",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-07T01:47:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you insert 2 SIMs of the same carrier into a DSDS device, then maybe the same UID could have priviledge on both subIds (and slots). In this case, if the Carrier App filed 2 restricted network requests for the two subIDs and lost one of it, then both restricted network requests will be cleared. I don\u0027t think it is a good idea to call SubscriptionManager.getSubscriptionId(mLogicalSlot) because it may give you the new subID which belongs to another UID. \n\nI don\u0027t understand how moving CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the CS handler thread could solve this issue, since when CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator got the notification that uid0 has lost the CarrierPrivilege on slot0, the corresponding subID of slot0 should have disappeared.",
      "parentUuid": "4cd93e74_9e7e4895",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3abc9a9_5e126d33",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T09:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, it would be possible to get the subId corresponding to the logical slot here, by calling SubscriptionManager.getSubscriptionId(mLogicalSlot)? There\u0027s still a race here, but maybe better than the alternatives?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 210,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f62f25ba_69913f30",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.java",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-06T15:04:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When does the mapping of \"slot -\u003e subId\" change?\nIs there any relationship with simConfigChanged or onCarrierServiceChanged?\n\nIf there are no relationship, I think we can use `getSubscriptionId` to get subId and call Connectivity callback with pair of uid and subId so that ConnectivityService does not need to call back CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator from `handleUidCarrierPrivilegesLost` \n\nIf there are relationship, we need to be careful not to get the wrong subId.\nIn this case, \"move CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to the CS handler thread\" option could be easier than getting correct uid and subId pair.",
      "parentUuid": "d3abc9a9_5e126d33",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 210,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "5aaa20364eed279656d8be6a12e40ee39198cd79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
